{"availability":"available","full":"firsttris/vscode-jest-runner","name":"vscode-jest-runner","description":"VS Code extension to run and debug Jest, Vitest, Playwright, Rstest, Bun, Deno and Node.js tests with one click. CodeLens above every test, native Test Explorer, code coverage, watch mode, monorepo and Create React App support. Zero configuration: reads your jest.config, vitest.config and playwright.config.","category":"Developer tools","language":"TypeScript","stars":304,"forks":142,"created":"2017-12-29T15:58:24Z","updated":"2026-10-08T22:22:29Z","license":"MIT","branch":"master","homepage":"https://firsttris.github.io/vscode-jest-runner/","topics":["bun","code-coverage","debugging","deno","e2e-testing","javascript","jest","monorepo","node-test-runner","playwright","rstest","test-explorer","test-runner","testing","typescript","unit-testing","visual-studio-code","vitest","vscode","vscode-extension"],"demo":"https://firsttris.github.io/vscode-jest-runner/","color":"#193546","ink":"#a6d6e8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:02.781Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:02.781Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:02.781Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-09T03:37:02.781Z","stars":304,"forks":142}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Jest Runner is a lightweight Visual Studio Code extension that lets you run a single test, a describe block or a whole test file without leaving the editor. It adds Run and Debug actions above every test (CodeLens), a native Test Explorer with code coverage, context menu entries and commands for the keyboard.","It started as a Jest test runner and grew into a universal JavaScript and TypeScript test runner for VS Code: it detects whether a file belongs to Jest, Vitest, Playwright, Rstest, Bun, Deno or the Node.js test runner and builds the right command for it. Monorepos, multiple configs, Create React App, Nx, Next.js, NestJS and Vite projects work out of the box.","💡 Why not the built-in runner of each framework? Jest Runner runs the real CLI of your project in a terminal or the debugger, with your config, your environment and your Node version. Nothing is emulated, so what passes here passes in CI."],"features":["Debug with breakpoints, variable inspection and the call stack","Watch mode for automatic re-runs while you code","Update snapshots with one command","Re-run the previous test with a keyboard shortcut","Inline coverage in the editor via the VS Code coverage API"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/firsttris/vscode-jest-runner/blob/master/README.md","fingerprint":"4c9fbade5ca88300cbb9543ee103a226a250ddccc086c2feca2d3a7ee02e0f06","extractedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:02.936Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:02.936Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Jest Runner is a lightweight Visual Studio Code extension that lets you run a single test, a describe block or a whole test file without leaving the editor. It adds Run and Debug actions above every test (CodeLens), a native Test Explorer with code coverage, context menu entries and commands for the keyboard.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/firsttris/vscode-jest-runner/blob/master/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"4c9fbade5ca88300cbb9543ee103a226a250ddccc086c2feca2d3a7ee02e0f06","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/firsttris/vscode-jest-runner/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:02.936Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-08T22:22:29Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/firsttris/vscode-jest-runner/blob/master/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-09T03:37:02.937Z","hash":"4c9fbade5ca88300cbb9543ee103a226a250ddccc086c2feca2d3a7ee02e0f06","originalBytes":16101,"storedBytes":16101,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["test","jest","run","runner","debug","code","coverage","command","file","tests","bun","vitest","config","does","one","open","rstest","what","configs","deno","explorer","framework","frameworks","node.js","playwright"